  data: {
    LLM: 'Game: Aggravation Speed. Flow: setup split, simultaneous race with deal/play cover actions, valid aggravation call ends game.',
    Player: 'Aggravation Speed is a two-player reflex race: cover matching ranks fast, then call Aggravation when your deck is gone and a match is live.',
    objective: "Be first to empty your deck and legally call 'Aggravation!' on a live match.",
    gameplay: "Players simultaneously extend rows from their decks. Any time equal ranks appear anywhere in layout, a player may cover matching cards with new cards from own deck. Cascades continue while matches exist. When no matches remain, both extend rows again. A player with empty deck wins by tapping a valid match and calling 'Aggravation!'.",
    keyRules: [
      'Play is simultaneous, not turn-based.',
      'Matches are by rank only; suits are irrelevant.',
      'If no matches exist, rows are extended equally until a match appears.',
      'A player with one last card must use it on a match, then find another match to call win.',
      'If one player is out and no match exists, opponent continues dealing until a match appears.',
    ],
